  "implementation": [
    "ScopedExecutor carries actual lexical caller frames into nested body INSERT execution. The row executor attaches these frames only to input reads. Newly invoked trigger programs retain their fresh event-specific OLD/NEW frames, so an outer NEW cannot satisfy an invalid NEW reference inside a DELETE program.",
    "Nested INSERTs, including ones without matching target programs, use the common typed ordinary input evaluator. Single-VALUES evaluates only used targets in physical-column order; duplicate rowid/ordinary targets retain existing last/first selection. Scalar query values and real JSON subtypes reach actual BEFORE/AFTER frames without conversion to untyped literals.",
    "Matching catalog programs materialize multiple VALUES sources before row programs. A source without matching programs streams its rows but evaluates every field, including discarded ones, before target mapping. Counters and last_insert_rowid retain actual source-row timing.",
    "BEFORE candidates still evaluate rowids in separate phases. Reached scalar query registers are retained; an independently observed native control disproves the blanket inside-trigger cache disable. Ordinary INSERTs without BEFORE avoid provisional generated/STRICT execution, retaining the existing actual point write checks."
  ],
  "reference_protocol": "Complete stdout/exit/first-error and independently observed persisted catalog/table/integrity contents compare with pinned SQLite 3.53.4 in rollback and WAL modes. Twelve generated nested cases have a new final-checkpoint seed; every earlier suite is rerun with fresh generated inputs. Four native correlation controls are retained separately as exploratory evidence. No skips, expected-output rewrites or native production routing are used.",
  "crash_scope": "SIGKILL timing samples for nested trigger INSERT writes to three tables, actual lexical OLD/NEW captures and a uniquely indexed target. Public Lean recovery followed by independent SQLite catalog/root-zero/rowid/schema-cookie/row/integrity checks. Complete old or new states are required. No every-syscall, power-loss or arbitrary-schedule claim.",
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned insert.c ordinary/source registers and program-dependent materialization; expr.c scalar subroutine reuse and Once registers. Native controls distinguish scalar-query results from live surrounding counters and preserve the negative cache-disable result.",
  "proof_scope": "All retained Core/file/physical and signed-counter contracts compile. An audited inputScope_empty law states that no lexical caller frames leaves the original read callback unchanged. A new executable group checks captured NEW, discarded-expression laziness, generated values, actual JSON subtype and caller counter/context restoration. No whole-trigger or SQLite equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, RAISE, recursive_triggers settings, triggered UPSERT, trigger-aware ALTER, writable CTEs and wider query/constraint/error combinations remain work. The maintained nested INSERT suite does not exhaust all inputs.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
